# Use shadcn/ui for UI

All interactive and form UI in this app must use the project's shadcn components under `app/components/ui/`.

## Required

- Forms: `Input`, `Textarea`, `Label`, `Select`, `Combobox`, `Button`, `Checkbox`/`Switch` (when added), and `InputGroup` for compound fields (value + unit/mode addon).
- Overlays: `Dialog`, `Popover`, `DropdownMenu` — not browser `alert`/`confirm` for product flows.
- Layout primitives already in the design system: `Card`, `Tabs`, `Separator`, `Collapsible`.
- Compose with `InputGroup` + `InputGroupInput` + `InputGroupAddon` when an input has a linked control (%, currency, mode select, icon, button).

## Do not

- Do not add raw `<select>`, unstyled `<button>`, or one-off form control CSS that duplicates shadcn primitives.
- Do not introduce another component library for the same jobs (MUI, Ant, plain HTML form kits).
- Do not style native inputs to "look like" shadcn — use the shared components.

## When a primitive is missing

1. Add the shadcn component into `app/components/ui/` (match existing token styles: rounded-xl, `--color-line`, accent focus ring).
2. Then use it in the feature.

## Exceptions

- Semantic HTML for accessibility (`label` via `Label`, file inputs may stay native and be triggered by a shadcn `Button`).
- Print-only layouts may use inline styles for print reliability.
